  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Shell",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3ac3c5524336-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 23,
                "start": 23
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Shell argues that the PMPA defines a \u201cfranchise\u201d by three elements: the supply of fuel, the use of the leased premises, and the use of the trademark."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Shell",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3ac3c5524336-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 23,
                "start": 23
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Shell contends that a dealer who remains on a gas\u2011station premises with the Shell sign but without fuel is effectively terminated under the statute."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Shell",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3ac3c5524336-0001-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 35,
                "start": 35
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Shell, shell proposes a test for termination: whether the conduct has effectively eliminated an essential component of one of the three franchise elements."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Shell\u2019s Position",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Dealers",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3ac3c5524336-0002-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 41,
                "start": 41
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Dealers maintain that an injunction is a form of relief to protect the franchisee, but the existence of a claim under the PMPA does not depend on whether the franchisee seeks an injunction."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Dealers",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3ac3c5524336-0002-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 49,
                "start": 48
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Dealers argue that the statute does not require injunctive relief as a prerequisite for a claim; the remedy is available but not mandatory."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Dealers",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3ac3c5524336d6f6faaa187ad300efe6dd5fa95ea0d429dab75de6c252c57462",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3ac3c5524336-0002-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 45,
                "start": 44
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Dealers contend that the statutory remedy includes injunctive relief, but they did not pursue it; the lower standard and lack of a need to show irreparable harm protect the franchisee under a federal cause of action."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Dealers\u2019 Position",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
